tasks.starter:
// CacheModule owns CacheService.
// FeatureModule needs it but got 'Nest can't resolve dependencies',
// so it was 'fixed' like this:
//
// @Module({
//   controllers: [FeatureController],
//   providers: [FeatureService, CacheService], // <-- the shortcut
// })
// export class FeatureModule {}
//
// Why does the shared cache now behave inconsistently, and what is the correct wiring?

model.en:
Re-listing CacheService in FeatureModule's providers makes Nest instantiate a SECOND, independent CacheService scoped to FeatureModule. Providers are singletons per scope, not globally — so FeatureModule's cache and CacheModule's cache are two different objects with separate in-memory state. Writes through one are invisible to the other, which is exactly the 'mysterious miss.' The error was real (the provider was private), but the shortcut traded a startup error for a silent correctness bug. Correct wiring: keep CacheService declared once, in CacheModule, and export it; then import CacheModule wherever it's needed.

@Module({ providers: [CacheService], exports: [CacheService] })
export class CacheModule {}

@Module({
  imports: [CacheModule],
  controllers: [FeatureController],
  providers: [FeatureService], // NOT CacheService
})
export class FeatureModule {}

Now every importer shares the one CacheService singleton.

model.ru:
Пере-перечисление CacheService в providers у FeatureModule заставляет Nest создать ВТОРОЙ, независимый CacheService в области видимости FeatureModule. Provider-ы — синглтоны на область видимости, а не глобально, — поэтому кэш FeatureModule и кэш CacheModule это два разных объекта с раздельным in-memory состоянием. Записи через один невидимы другому — это и есть «загадочный промах». Ошибка была настоящей (provider был приватным), но костыль обменял ошибку старта на тихий баг корректности. Правильная обвязка: объяви CacheService один раз, в CacheModule, и экспортируй его; затем импортируй CacheModule везде, где он нужен.

@Module({ providers: [CacheService], exports: [CacheService] })
export class CacheModule {}

@Module({
  imports: [CacheModule],
  controllers: [FeatureController],
  providers: [FeatureService], // НЕ CacheService
})
export class FeatureModule {}

Теперь каждый импортирующий разделяет один синглтон CacheService.

model.en:
@Controller('invoices')
export class InvoicesController {
  constructor(private readonly invoices: InvoiceService) {}
  @Post() create(@Body() dto: CreateInvoiceDto) { return this.invoices.create(dto); }
  @Get(':id') findOne(@Param('id') id: string) { return this.invoices.findOne(id); }
  @Get() list(@Query() q: ListInvoicesDto) { return this.invoices.list(q); }
}

@Injectable() export class InvoiceService { /* business logic + persistence; may use PdfService */ }
@Injectable() export class PdfService { /* renders PDF; internal to billing */ }

@Module({
  controllers: [InvoicesController],
  providers: [InvoiceService, PdfService],
  exports: [InvoiceService], // PdfService stays private
})
export class BillingModule {}

@Module({
  imports: [BillingModule], // grants access to the exported InvoiceService only
  providers: [NotificationsService],
})
export class NotificationsModule {}

The controller is a thin HTTP adapter; both services hold the logic; the boundary exports just InvoiceService so NotificationsModule can inject it while PdfService remains encapsulated inside billing.

